<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chao Mom Kham Le</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dao Shixun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chao Mom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kham">Kham</a> Le, known in Chinese as Dao Shixun, was the last hereditary ruler (chao phaendin) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tai-lu-people">Tai Lue</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xishuangbanna">Sipsong Panna</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>. He succeeded as a young man in the 1940s, and after the Communist victory in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> the old monarchy was replaced in 1953 by the Xishuangbanna Dai Autonomous Prefecture. He then served as an official of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> in Yunnan.</p></div>
